{"id": "2026-11-09-news-kremlin-rules-europeans-out-of-abu-dhabi-talks", "date": "2026-11-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Kremlin rules Europeans out of Abu Dhabi talks", "summary": "Kremlin says Abu Dhabi Ukraine talks on 10-11 November will be strictly trilateral, rejecting French statement that Europeans will be represented.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/live/2026/11/09/en-direct-guerre-en-ukraine-a-l-approche-de-pourparlers-a-abou-dhabi-volodymyr-zelensky-dit-s-etre-coordonne-avec-ursula-von-der-leyen_6808609_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "The Kremlin said on Monday 9 November that this week's Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi, set for Tuesday 10 and Wednesday 11 November, will be strictly \"trilateral\" between Russia, Ukraine and the US, a day after France said Europeans would be represented. French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said on Sunday 8 November that the E3 (France, Germany and the UK) would send their national security advisers, and that the European Commission would send Ursula von der Leyen's chief of staff, Björn Seibert. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov answered that the Americans and Ukrainians \"have their own channels\" to the Europeans. These are the first three-way talks since the US-Israeli war on Iran began on 28 February; an earlier Abu Dhabi round this year made no progress on territory. G7 foreign ministers meet in Paris on 9–10 November, partly so Europe can push for a seat at the table. Their worry is a CBS interview in which Donald Trump said Ukraine would \"end up with a little bit different shape\", meaning altered borders.", "why": "who sits in the room decides whether a deal over European security, and Ukraine's borders, is made without Europe.", "thread_id": "2026-11-09-news-kremlin-rules-europeans-out-of-abu-dhabi-talks", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-09", "event_date": "2026-11-10", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Russia", "Ukraine", "Abu Dhabi", "Kremlin", "G7"]}
{"id": "2026-11-09-news-qatar-s-premier-carries-iran-file-to-white-house", "date": "2026-11-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Qatar's premier carries Iran file to White House", "summary": "Trump hosts Qatar's PM on 9 November amid Qatari mediation of an Iranian proposal; Rubio sees no progress.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/9/qatar-pm-to-meet-trump-whats-the-latest-on-us-iran-negotiations", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Donald Trump was due to host Qatar's prime minister and foreign minister, Sheikh Mohammed bin Abdulrahman Al Thani, at the White House on Monday 9 November, as Qatar carries messages between Washington and Tehran. On Thursday 5 November Iran sent a new nuclear and peace proposal through Qatari mediators. Tehran says it will only discuss the plan once the US accepts its seven preconditions, including sanctions relief, and the US says it is examining it. Trump said strikes are unlikely \"if talks keep moving\", but Secretary of State Marco Rubio says he sees no progress. On Sunday 8 November Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi warned that Tehran would \"rain down hell\" if US attacks resume. The International Atomic Energy Agency (the UN nuclear watchdog) puts Iran's stock of uranium enriched to 60% at 440.9 kg; weapons-grade is about 90%.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-09-news-qatar-s-premier-carries-iran-file-to-white-house", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-09", "event_date": "2026-11-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Qatar", "Iran", "Donald Trump", "Marco Rubio"]}
{"id": "2026-11-09-news-trump-calls-deportations-too-tough-hires-miller", "date": "2026-11-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Trump calls deportations 'too tough', hires Miller", "summary": "Trump told CBS his deportation policy might be too tough for voters, then appointed Stephen Miller chief of staff.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/us-president-donald-trump-says-deportation-policy-was-too-tough-for-voters/a-79895321", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "In his first big interview since Republicans lost both houses of Congress in the midterms, Donald Trump told CBS on Sunday 8 November that his deportation policy \"might be too tough\" for voters and that an immigration deal with Democrats is \"doable\". He gave no details. Shortly after the interview he made Stephen Miller, the main architect of the hardline deportation drive, his chief of staff. That appointment points the opposite way from the softer words.", "why": "the new Congress will test whether any deal materialises. The White House's choice of staff is a better guide to policy than what Trump said on TV.", "thread_id": "2026-11-09-news-trump-calls-deportations-too-tough-hires-miller", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-09", "event_date": "2026-11-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Donald Trump", "Stephen Miller", "US Congress"]}
{"id": "2026-11-09-news-paris-donors-chase-chernobyl-arch-repair-money", "date": "2026-11-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Paris donors chase Chernobyl arch repair money", "summary": "France, Ukraine and EBRD open Paris donor conference for Chernobyl arch repairs; 260m of 500m euros raised.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/live/2026/11/09/en-direct-guerre-en-ukraine-a-l-approche-de-pourparlers-a-abou-dhabi-volodymyr-zelensky-dit-s-etre-coordonne-avec-ursula-von-der-leyen_6808609_3210.html#chernobyl", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Kremlin said on Monday 9 November that this week's Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi, set for Tuesday 10 and Wednesday 11 November, will be strictly \"trilateral\" between Russia, Ukraine and the US, a day after France said Europeans would be represented. French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said on Sunday 8 November that the E3 (France, Germany and the UK) would send their national security advisers, and that the European Commission would send Ursula von der Leyen's chief of staff, Björn Seibert. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov answered that the Americans and Ukrainians \"have their own channels\" to the Europeans. These are the first three-way talks since the US-Israeli war on Iran began on 28 February; an earlier Abu Dhabi round this year made no progress on territory. G7 foreign ministers meet in Paris on 9–10 November, partly so Europe can push for a seat at the table. Their worry is a CBS interview in which Donald Trump said Ukraine would \"end up with a little bit different shape\", meaning altered borders.", "why": "who sits in the room decides whether a deal over European security, and Ukraine's borders, is made without Europe.", "thread_id": "2026-11-09-news-paris-donors-chase-chernobyl-arch-repair-money", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-09", "event_date": "2026-11-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Chernobyl", "EBRD", "France", "Ukraine"]}
{"id": "2026-11-09-news-cop31-opens-in-antalya-without-the-us", "date": "2026-11-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "COP31 opens in Antalya without the US", "summary": "UN climate summit COP31 opens in Antalya on 9 November with no US delegation; Turkey pushes 35-by-35 electrification pledge.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/sciences/environnement/la-cop31-s-ouvre-en-turquie-sur-fond-de-crise-energetique-et-d-absence-americaine", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "COP31, the annual UN climate summit, opened on Monday 9 November in Antalya, Turkey, with nearly 200 countries and over 100,000 participants expected over two weeks, and with no US delegation. The host is putting electrification at the centre with a non-binding \"35 by 35\" pledge: electricity should supply at least 35% of global energy demand by 2035, up from about a fifth today according to the International Energy Agency. The talks open against an energy-price crisis caused by the Iran war, a shortfall in climate-adaptation money, and forecasts that 2026 will be one of the four hottest years on record.", "why": "expectations are low. The test is whether earlier pledges turn into concrete, funded measures.", "thread_id": "2026-11-09-news-cop31-opens-in-antalya-without-the-us", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-09", "event_date": "2026-11-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["COP31", "Turkey", "Antalya"]}
{"id": "2026-11-09-news-merz-backs-aigner-for-german-president", "date": "2026-11-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Merz backs Aigner for German president", "summary": "Merz endorses CSU's Ilse Aigner to succeed Steinmeier as German federal president.", "url": "https://www.tagesschau.de/inland/innenpolitik/aigner-bundespraesidentin-100.html", "source_domain": "tagesschau.de", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "German Chancellor Friedrich Merz said on Sunday 8 November that he backs Ilse Aigner of the Bavarian CSU, president of the Bavarian state parliament, as the next federal president, succeeding Frank-Walter Steinmeier early next year. The CDU leadership endorsed her on Sunday evening, and the party's federal executive and a joint press appearance were due on Monday 9 November. The SPD and Greens have already signalled support. If the Federal Convention (the body of MPs and state delegates that elects the president) confirms her, she would be Germany's first female head of state.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-09-news-merz-backs-aigner-for-german-president", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-09", "event_date": "2026-11-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ilse Aigner", "Friedrich Merz", "CSU", "Germany"]}
{"id": "2026-11-09-news-just-eat-cuts-373-swiss-delivery-jobs", "date": "2026-11-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Just Eat cuts 373 Swiss delivery jobs", "summary": "Just Eat confirms cutting 373 of about 700 Swiss jobs, moving to a flexible courier model unions call bogus self-employment.", "url": "https://www.unia.ch/de/medien/medienmitteilungen/mitteilung/a/24934", "source_domain": "unia.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Food-delivery company Just Eat confirmed on Monday 9 November that it is cutting 373 of its roughly 700 jobs in Switzerland: 193 directly employed couriers and 180 agency workers in Zurich, Winterthur, Bern, Biel, Fribourg and St. Gallen. The company says its shift-based model is no longer competitive and it will move to a \"more flexible\" delivery model. Talks on a social plan are still under way. The unions Unia and Syndicom call the new model bogus self-employment that avoids labour and social-insurance law. They point to the Zurich social-insurance office (SVA), which said last week that platforms cannot choose their workers' status themselves. The unions want the cantons and the State Secretariat for Economic Affairs (SECO) to step in.", "why": "this follows SRF's late-October report on Uber Eats pushing local bike couriers out of the market. Whether authorities enforce employee status will decide what delivery work in Switzerland looks like.", "thread_id": "2026-11-09-news-just-eat-cuts-373-swiss-delivery-jobs", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-09", "event_date": "2026-11-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Just Eat", "Unia", "Syndicom", "SECO"]}
{"id": "2026-11-09-news-38-of-apprentices-reach-tertiary-degree", "date": "2026-11-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "38% of apprentices reach tertiary degree", "summary": "FSO: 38% of 2012 CFC holders obtained a tertiary qualification within 12 years, strongly dependent on parental education.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/6AuqBK0VXkKN", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Thirty-eight percent of people who earned a federal apprenticeship certificate (CFC/EFZ) in 2012 had a tertiary qualification 12 years later, the Federal Statistical Office reported on Monday 9 November. The most common routes were a federal professional diploma (15%), a higher vocational college (12%) and a bachelor's from a university of applied sciences or a university of teacher education (9%). Rates ranged from 59% in nursing to 23% in retail and personal services, and from 30% at micro-firms to 43% at large firms. Family background mattered most: the rate was over 50% when a parent had a tertiary degree, and 27% when neither parent had finished upper-secondary school.", "why": "it puts a number on how open the apprenticeship-to-higher-education route really is, and on how much it still depends on parents.", "thread_id": "2026-11-09-news-38-of-apprentices-reach-tertiary-degree", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-09", "event_date": "2026-11-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Statistical Office", "CFC"]}
{"id": "2026-11-09-news-vaud-overhauls-its-tax-administration", "date": "2026-11-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Vaud overhauls its tax administration", "summary": "Vaud reorganises its tax administration by 2028 after a BDO governance audit ordered over the bouclier fiscal affair.", "url": "https://www.vd.ch/actualites/communiques-de-presse-de-letat-de-vaud/detail/communique/une-administration-reorganisee-et-modernisee-pour-porter-les-grandes-reformes-fiscales", "source_domain": "vd.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Vaud's finance department announced on Monday 9 November that it will reorganise the canton's tax administration (DGF) by 2028, based on a governance audit by BDO that was published the same day. The audit was ordered in August 2025 after the controversy over how the canton applied its \"bouclier fiscal\" (a tax cap). It found the DGF does its job as required, but recommended a phased overhaul of strategy, governance, processes and communication. This is the first step in a programme running to 2032 that is meant to prepare the canton for major tax reforms.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-09-news-vaud-overhauls-its-tax-administration", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-09", "event_date": "2026-11-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Vaud", "DGF", "BDO"]}
